1
00:00:00,930 --> 00:00:04,330
A playable tour of your six Python
components.

2
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:07,730
Story & actions explains every move as it
happens.

3
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:11,130
The AI log records each step and why.

4
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:14,530
Live code follows the running Python line
by line.

5
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:17,930
Learn: Data flow, code, reference,
components.

6
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:21,330
Data flow shows how seed becomes a level.

7
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:24,730
Components lists roles and what depends on
each.

8
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:28,130
Test yourself: Explain it back and Edge
cases.

9
00:00:28,130 --> 00:00:31,530
Enough touring — let’s play.

10
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:34,930
Move with the arrow keys — or WASD.

11
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:38,330
Walls and obstacles gently stop you.

12
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:41,730
Step onto a gem — the score ticks up.

13
00:00:41,730 --> 00:00:45,130
Get next to an enemy, press E to engage.

14
00:00:45,130 --> 00:00:48,530
It costs a turn plus the bounty penalty.

15
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:51,930
That’s the core loop — try any level!

16
00:00:51,930 --> 00:00:55,330
On phones, a D-pad appears under the
board.

17
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:58,730
Tap the arrows to move around the grid.

18
00:00:58,730 --> 00:01:02,130
Everything else works exactly the same.

19
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:05,530
Slow the speed to 0.7s to follow along.

20
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:08,930
Watch AI lets the planner run the level
for you.

21
00:01:08,930 --> 00:01:12,330
Watch the frontier of states it explores.

22
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:15,730
Pause to freeze and inspect a state.

23
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:19,130
Step advances exactly one AI turn.

24
00:01:19,130 --> 00:01:22,781
Resume picks right back up.

25
00:01:22,781 --> 00:01:26,431
Resume picks right back up.

26
00:01:26,431 --> 00:01:30,082
Resume picks right back up.

27
00:01:30,082 --> 00:01:33,732
Resume picks right back up.

28
00:01:33,732 --> 00:01:37,132
At the exit, the summary card appears.

29
00:01:37,132 --> 00:01:41,931
Close it anytime — the board stays live.

30
00:01:41,931 --> 00:01:45,331
Live code highlights the currently
executing line.

31
00:01:45,331 --> 00:01:48,731
Step line walks the cursor through the
trace.

32
00:01:48,731 --> 00:01:52,131
Run-to-next-function jumps to the next
call.

33
00:01:52,131 --> 00:01:55,531
Scrub to replay any earlier moment.

34
00:01:55,531 --> 00:01:58,931
Variables panel tracks values as they
change.

35
00:01:58,931 --> 00:02:02,331
That’s how you read the code visually.

36
00:02:02,331 --> 00:02:05,731
Data flow shows how a seed becomes a
level.

37
00:02:05,731 --> 00:02:09,346
Click any stage to see what it produces.

38
00:02:09,346 --> 00:02:12,746
Read code opens the annotated full source.

39
00:02:12,746 --> 00:02:16,146
Reference gives printable per-file sheets.

40
00:02:16,146 --> 00:02:19,546
Components lays out roles and
dependencies.

41
00:02:19,546 --> 00:02:22,946
Explain it back quizzes you on each file.

42
00:02:22,946 --> 00:02:26,346
Pick a file and answer a question.

43
00:02:26,346 --> 00:02:29,746
Answer, then compare to the model answer.

44
00:02:29,746 --> 00:02:33,146
Highlight jumps to the exact lines in the
source.

45
00:02:33,146 --> 00:02:36,546
Edge cases lists known quirks — tagged
honestly.

46
00:02:36,546 --> 00:02:39,946
Customize the look to your taste.

47
00:02:39,946 --> 00:02:43,346
Toggle light and dark theme.

48
00:02:43,346 --> 00:02:46,746
Fit scales the board to your window.

49
00:02:46,746 --> 00:02:50,146
Random generates a level from a fresh
seed.

50
00:02:50,146 --> 00:02:53,546
Reset clears the run and starts clean.

51
00:02:53,546 --> 00:02:56,946
Or pick one of seven baked levels.

52
00:02:56,946 --> 00:03:00,346
Then Watch AI solves it.

53
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:03,746
That’s the whole explainer.

54
00:03:03,746 --> 00:03:07,146
Play, watch, read, quiz, present — enjoy.

55
00:03:07,146 --> 00:03:10,546
Thanks for watching!

